WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:07.720
Put an electrode inside a resting frog muscle fibre, at the end plate where the

2
00:00:07.720 --> 00:00:09.780
nerve ends. Stimulate nothing.

3
00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:13.320
Small depolarizations still arrive at random times.

4
00:00:13.860 --> 00:00:17.800
Each is about the same size, and each is far too small to fire the fibre.

5
00:00:18.440 --> 00:00:19.440
What are they?

6
00:00:19.783 --> 00:00:22.383
These are miniature end plate potentials.

7
00:00:22.803 --> 00:00:27.083
Fatt and cats attributed them to spontaneous release of acetylcholine from the nerve

8
00:00:27.083 --> 00:00:32.483
terminal. Del Castillo and cats asked whether a nerve impulse evokes the same units.

9
00:00:33.123 --> 00:00:37.883
They bathed the frog junction in less calcium and more magnesium, which cut release

10
00:00:37.883 --> 00:00:42.663
to a trickle. Now an impulse often produced nothing at all, a failure.

11
00:00:43.567 --> 00:00:46.207
When a response did come, its size was not random.

12
00:00:46.887 --> 00:00:51.347
The amplitudes clustered at the size of one miniature, at twice that, and at three

13
00:00:51.347 --> 00:00:54.807
times that. So the evoked response came in packets.

14
00:00:55.627 --> 00:01:00.487
Each packet is a quantum, a packet of many molecules, later identified with the

15
00:01:00.487 --> 00:01:01.767
contents of one vesicle.

16
00:01:02.287 --> 00:01:04.507
It is not one molecule of acetylcholine.

17
00:01:05.300 --> 00:01:10.080
The mean quantal content is the average number of quanta -1 impulse releases.

18
00:01:10.660 --> 00:01:14.180
Take a made -up frog junction in low calcium and high magnesium.

19
00:01:14.920 --> 00:01:20.540
The mean miniature and the mean response, failures included, are both 0 .40

20
00:01:20.540 --> 00:01:24.380
millivolts. So the ratio is one quantum per stimulus.

21
00:01:24.380 --> 00:01:30.260
Failures give a second estimate, since 74 of 200 stimuli gave no response.

22
00:01:31.183 --> 00:01:37.943
Under a Poisson model, minus the natural log of 0 .37 is 0 .99, The two estimates

23
00:01:37.943 --> 00:01:44.463
agree. Now suppose 60 quanta of 0 .40 mV each in normal calcium.

24
00:01:45.063 --> 00:01:49.383
If they add linearly, that is 24 mV against a threshold of 12.

25
00:01:50.483 --> 00:01:53.163
Toy values; real frog values differ.

26
00:01:53.163 --> 00:01:57.323
The safety factor, the ratio of the two, is two.

27
00:01:58.067 --> 00:02:04.027
In myasthenia gravis, fewer receptors mean a smaller quantal size, and 60 of them

28
00:02:04.027 --> 00:02:05.087
still fire the fibre.

29
00:02:05.707 --> 00:02:10.127
But suppose release runs down by 25 percent, to 45 quanta.

30
00:02:10.727 --> 00:02:14.487
The response is then 10 .8 millivolts, and the fibre fails.

31
00:02:15.427 --> 00:02:20.487
Miniature size also depends on vesicle filling, so confirm with a receptor count.

32
00:02:21.007 --> 00:02:26.267
So smaller miniatures point to receptors or filling, and fewer packets point before

33
00:02:26.267 --> 00:02:26.927
the synapse.
